{%- comment -%}
  Head-level robots control for pages that must not be indexed by default.

  Why this lives in the head: a robots meta tag is only honoured inside
  <head>. A section renders in <body>, so a section-level robots tag is
  ignored by search engines. This snippet is rendered from
  layout/theme.liquid head, alongside the longeva schema snippets.

  Default-safe doorway-page guardrail (Brief v4 Section 12):
  the local-area town pages (Rochdale, Manchester, Oldham, Bury, Bolton,
  Blackburn, Salford, Near Me, Manchester Airport) are near-identical by
  nature. Google treats a single clinic spinning up many "travel clinic
  in [town]" pages as scaled/doorway content. So every page on the
  local-area template is noindex by default, purely from the template
  suffix (no per-page metafield needed to be safe).

  Opt a page IN to indexing only once it carries genuinely unique local
  content: set its page metafield custom.allow_index (boolean) to true.

  Service/vaccine PRODUCTS (page/product duplication clean-up): these
  products are Sesami booking objects, not SEO surfaces — the paired
  Shopify PAGE (e.g. page.service-page.json / longeva-service-layout.liquid)
  is the intended indexable landing content for the same treatment.
  longeva-service-layout-product.liquid and longeva-service-page.liquid
  render near-identical H1/body/FAQ/CTA structure to their page
  counterpart, so leaving both indexable is duplicate-content exposure.
  noindex by default on the service/vaccine product templates; follow is
  kept so Sesami's own scripts and any internal links stay fully
  crawlable — only indexing is blocked, nothing about the booking flow.

  A few products (Adrenaline Nasal Spray, Jet Lag, Thrush, per the
  service-layout-product.liquid comment) have NO sibling page and are
  the only indexable surface for that service. Opt those IN via product
  metafield custom.allow_index (boolean) = true — this has NOT been set
  for you here, since which products are page-less is an Admin content
  question, not something theme code can determine. Until that metafield
  is set, those specific products will be noindexed along with the rest.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign noindex = false

  comment
    Local-area town pages: noindex by default (template), opt IN via
    custom.allow_index. See above.
  endcomment
  if template.suffix == 'local-area'
    assign noindex = true
    if page.metafields.custom.allow_index.value == true
      assign noindex = false
    endif
  endif

  comment
    Structural shells (Brief v4): a page is created published so navigation
    resolves and the structure is testable, but carries custom.noindex = true
    until its content lands, so an empty page is never indexed. Clear the
    metafield (or set it false) once Alicia or Varsha have filled the page.
  endcomment
  if page.metafields.custom.noindex.value == true
    assign noindex = true
  endif

  comment
    Service/vaccine booking products: noindex by default (template), opt
    IN via product metafield custom.allow_index for page-less services.
    See above.
  endcomment
  if template.suffix == 'service' or template.suffix == 'vaccine'
    assign noindex = true
    if product.metafields.custom.allow_index.value == true
      assign noindex = false
    endif
  endif
-%}
{%- if noindex -%}
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow">
{%- endif -%}
